{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_mismatch_1.march","start_line":10,"start_col":14,"end_line":10,"end_col":30,"message":"`read` takes a `Cap(IO.FileRead)` parameter, but capability values were retired: a function no longer receives its authority, it uses the current authority, which `main`'s `needs` clause asks for and each operation checks.\nhelp: remove the parameter and the argument at each call; to state what `read` may use, give it a `needs` clause.","code":"cap_param_retired","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":10,"start_col":10,"end_line":10,"end_col":30,"text":""},{"kind":"replace","start_line":12,"start_col":47,"end_line":12,"end_col":48,"text":""}],"applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/cap_mismatch_1.march","start_line":12,"start_col":14,"end_line":12,"end_col":29,"message":"`main` asks for its authority with `Cap` parameters, which are deprecated and will be removed in the next release: a capability value grants nothing since the current authority replaced it.\nhelp: request it with a `needs` clause: `fn main() needs IO.Console do`.","code":"deprecated_main_cap","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":12,"start_col":9,"end_line":12,"end_col":30,"text":"()"},{"kind":"replace","start_line":12,"start_col":31,"end_line":12,"end_col":31,"text":"needs IO.Console "}],"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/cap_mismatch_1.march","start_line":12,"start_col":47,"end_line":12,"end_col":48,"message":"`read` needs file-read access, but `c` is the console capability.","code":"cap_mismatch:IO.FileRead","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"insert","after_line":7,"text":"  needs IO.FileRead"},{"kind":"replace","start_line":12,"start_col":47,"end_line":12,"end_col":48,"text":"_cap_fileread"},{"kind":"replace","start_line":12,"start_col":29,"end_line":12,"end_col":29,"text":", _cap_fileread : Cap(IO.FileRead)"}],"applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_1.march","start_line":12,"start_col":42,"end_line":12,"end_col":49,"message":"`read` needs `Cap(IO.FileRead)`"},{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_1.march","start_line":12,"start_col":10,"end_line":12,"end_col":11,"message":"`c` was bound here as `Cap(IO.Console)`"},{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_1.march","start_line":10,"start_col":2,"end_line":10,"end_col":51,"message":"`Cap(IO.FileRead)` is named here, and the module declares no `needs IO.FileRead`"},{"file":"errors/cap_mismatch_1.march","start_line":12,"start_col":9,"end_line":12,"end_col":30,"message":"`main` is granted only `Cap(IO.Console)` here"}],"notes":["`IO.Console` and `IO.FileRead` are both parts of `IO`; neither contains the other.","help: give `main` a `Cap(IO.FileRead)` parameter and pass it to `read`.","and add `needs IO.FileRead` to the module."],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
